wlr_egl_buffer: finish the buffer when it is destroyed

Every wlr_buffer implementation must call wlr_buffer_finish() from its
destroy hook (wlroots 0.17+): that emits the destroy signal and destroys
the buffer's addons. The libmali wl_buffer wrapper never did, so the DRM
backend's KMS framebuffer addon (and its imported GEM object, a whole
640x480 frame) outlived every buffer a libmali client ever presented.
On a 1 GB RK3326 handheld each fullscreen app launch (a game, the
launcher itself) left 3 framebuffers behind, about 3.7 MB, until the
compositor ran the board out of memory.

--- a/types/wlr_egl_buffer.c
+++ b/types/wlr_egl_buffer.c
@@ -64,8 +64,11 @@
 static void egl_buffer_destroy(struct wlr_buffer *wlr_buffer) {
 	struct wlr_egl_buffer *buffer =
 		wl_container_of(wlr_buffer, buffer, base);
-	wl_list_remove(&buffer->resource_destroy.link);
 	wl_list_remove(&buffer->release.link);
+
+	wlr_buffer_finish(wlr_buffer);
+
+	wl_list_remove(&buffer->resource_destroy.link);
 	free(buffer);
 }
 
